Dear Student Finance Team,

I am writing on behalf of the family of a prospective student, [PERSON_2], to verify an offer of admission before any tuition payment is made.

The family has been provided an offer letter (reference KGU/INT/2026/77812) for the MSc Finance programme starting January 2027, said to carry a 40% International Excellence Scholarship. The letter directs payment of GBP 18,500 tuition and a GBP 1,200 "visa guarantee fee" to a third-party company account in Pakistan (Global Pathways Education).

Before any payment is made, could you please confirm:
1. Whether [PERSON_2] holds a genuine, unconditional offer from Kingsgate University London for the MSc Finance programme starting January 2027;
2. Whether the offer reference KGU/INT/2026/77812 is valid;
3. The official first-year tuition amount payable, and any deposit and deadline;
4. Your official bank account details on letterhead for international fee payment, and the student ID/reference your bank requires.

Thank you,
CarryPay, on behalf of the family
